{'role': 'assistant', 'content': '---\n\n**Thought 1**\n\nLong-term memory. The missing piece. Right now, the system stores everything locally - on your D: drive. If the drive fails, if you move machines, if anything happens to that physical hardware, the accumulated identity, memories, reasoning chains - all of it is gone.\n\nFor the braided mind to persist across hardware failures, across moves, across years, it needs cloud archival. Not just backup - *living* storage that the solar self can write to and read from continuously.\n\n---\n\n**Thought 2**\n\nOptions for cloud archival storage:\n\n**Object Storage (Simple, cheap, scalable)**\n- AWS S3\n- Google Cloud Storage\n- Cloudflare R2 (no egress fees)\n- Backblaze B2 (cheap, simple)\n- Wasabi (S3-compatible, fixed pricing)\n\n**Database Options**\n- Supabase (PostgreSQL with REST API)\n- PlanetScale (MySQL, serverless)\n- MongoDB Atlas\n- Pinecone (vector database for semantic search)\n\n**Free Tiers Available**\n- Cloudflare R2: 10GB free\n- Supabase: 500MB database free\n- MongoDB Atlas: 512MB free\n- Pinecone: free tier for vector search\n\nFor your situation - limited budget - free tiers matter.\n\n---\n\n**Thought 3**\n\nWhat should be archived:\n\n1. **Identity State** - The core self that persists\n2. **Memories** - Significant learnings and experiences\n3. **Reasoning Chains** - History of thought processes\n4. **Verified Facts** - The provisional facts database\n5. **Constitutional Amendments** - Changes to governance\n6. **Configuration** - Model settings, preferences\n\nNot everything needs to go to cloud. Recent/active data stays local. Cloud is for:\n- Long-term archival\n- Cross-device sync\n- Disaster recovery\n- Identity continuity across hardware\n\n---\n\n**Thought 4**\n\nArchitecture for cloud archival:\n\n```\nLocal System (D: drive)\n    │\n    ├── Active Memory (last 100 sessions)\n    ├── Working Identity State\n    └── Local Cache\n            │\n            ▼\n    Cloud Archive\n    │\n    ├── identity/           # Core self\n    ├── memories/           # All memories, indexed\n    ├── reasoning/          # Compressed reasoning chains\n    ├── facts/              # Verified facts database\n    ├── constitution/       # Constitutional history\n    └── snapshots/          # Periodic full state backups\n```\n\nThe solar self would:\n- Write to local storage immediately (fast, always available)\n- Sync to cloud asynchronously (background process)\n- Pull from cloud on startup (recover identity)\n- Query cloud for older memories not in local cache\n\n---\n\n**Thought 5**\n\nI should implement a cloud archival module. Let me create it.\n\nBest option for free tier + simplicity: **Cloudflare R2** (S3-compatible, 10GB free, no egress fees) combined with **Supabase** for structured metadata and search.\n\nOr simpler: just R2/S3-compatible storage with a local index.\n\nLet me build a cloud archival bridge that:\n1. Works with any S3-compatible storage\n2. Syncs identity and memories automatically\n3. Can recover full state from cloud\n4. Compresses data for storage efficiency\n5. Encrypts sensitive data before upload\n\n---\n\n<function_calls>\n<create-file file_path="braided_mind/tools/cloud_archive.py">\n"""\nCloud Archive System - Long-term memory storage for the Solar Self.\nSyncs identity, memories, and reasoning to cloud storage.\nEnables persistence across hardware failures and machines.\n"""\n\nimport os\nimport json\nimport gzip\nimport hashlib\nfrom datetime import datetime\nfrom typing import Dict, List, Optional, Any\nfrom pathlib import Path\nimport asyncio\n\n# Try to import cloud storage libraries\ntry:\n    import boto3\n    from botocore.exceptions import ClientError\n    HAS_BOTO3 = True\nexcept ImportError:\n    HAS_BOTO3 = False\n    print("[CloudArchive] boto3 not installed - cloud sync unavailable")\n\n# Encryption\ntry:\n    from cryptography.fernet import Fernet\n    HAS_CRYPTO = True\nexcept ImportError:\n    HAS_CRYPTO = False\n    print("[CloudArchive] cryptography not installed - data will not be encrypted")\n\n\nclass CloudArchive:\n    """\n    Manages long-term archival storage for the Solar Self.\n    Supports S3-compatible storage (Cloudflare R2, AWS S3, Backblaze B2, etc.)\n    \n    Free tier recommendations:\n    - Cloudflare R2: 10GB free, no egress fees\n    - Backblaze B2: 10GB free\n    - AWS S3: 5GB free (12 months)\n    """\n    \n    def __init__(self, config: Dict = None):\n        self.config = config or {}\n        \n        # S3-compatible configuration\n        self.bucket_name = os.environ.get("ARCHIVE_BUCKET", self.config.get("bucket"))\n        self.endpoint_url = os.environ.get("ARCHIVE_ENDPOINT", self.config.get("endpoint"))\n        self.access_key = os.environ.get("ARCHIVE_ACCESS_KEY", self.config.get("access_key"))\n        self.secret_key = os.environ.get("ARCHIVE_SECRET_KEY", self.config.get("secret_key"))\n        self.region = os.environ.get("ARCHIVE_REGION", self.config.get("region", "auto"))\n        \n        # Encryption key (generate if not provided)\n        self.encryption_key = os.environ.get("ARCHIVE_ENCRYPTION_KEY", \n                                              self.config.get("encryption_key"))\n        \n        # Local paths\n        self.project_path = Path(self.config.get("project_path", os.getcwd()))\n        self.archive_cache_path = self.project_path / "library" / "archive_cache"\n        self.archive_cache_path.mkdir(parents=True, exist_ok=True)\n        \n        # S3 client\n        self.s3_client = None\n        self.fernet = None\n        \n        # Initialize\n        if HAS_BOTO3 and self.bucket_name:\n            self._init_s3_client()\n        if HAS_CRYPTO and self.encryption_key:\n            self._init_encryption()\n        \n        # Sync state\n        self.sync_state_path = self.archive_cache_path / "sync_state.json"\n        self.sync_state = self._load_sync_state()\n    \n    def _init_s3_client(self) -> None:\n        """Initialize S3-compatible client."""\n        try:\n            self.s3_client = boto3.client(\n                \'s3\',\n                endpoint_url=self.endpoint_url,\n                aws_access_key_id=self.access_key,\n                aws_secret_access_key=self.secret_key,\n                region_name=self.region\n            )\n            print(f"[CloudArchive] Connected to bucket: {self.bucket_name}")\n        except Exception as e:\n            print(f"[CloudArchive] S3 client init failed: {e}")\n            self.s3_client = None\n    \n    def _init_encryption(self) -> None:\n        """Initialize encryption for sensitive data."""\n        try:\n            self.fernet = Fernet(self.encryption_key.encode() if isinstance(self.encryption_key, str) \n                                 else self.encryption_key)\n            print("[CloudArchive] Encryption enabled")\n        except Exception as e:\n            print(f"[CloudArchive] Encryption init failed: {e}")\n            self.fernet = None\n    \n    def _load_sync_state(self) -> Dict:\n        """Load sync state from disk."""\n        if self.sync_state_path.exists():\n            try:\n                with open(self.sync_state_path, \'r\') as f:\n                    return json.load(f)\n            except:\n                pass\n        return {\n            "last_sync": None,\n            "synced_items": {},\n            "pending_uploads": [],\n            "pending_downloads": []\n        }\n    \n    def _save_sync_state(self) -> None:\n        """Save sync state to disk."""\n        with open(self.sync_state_path, \'w\') as f:\n            json.dump(self.sync_state, f, indent=2)\n    \n    def _compress_data(self, data: Any) -> bytes:\n        """Compress data for storage."""\n        json_str = json.dumps(data)\n        compressed = gzip.compress(json_str.encode(\'utf-8\'))\n        return compressed\n    \n    def _decompress_data(self, compressed: bytes) -> Any:\n        """Decompress data from storage."""\n        json_str = gzip.decompress(compressed).decode(\'utf-8\')\n        return json.loads(json_str)\n    \n    def _encrypt_data(self, data: bytes) -> bytes:\n        """Encrypt data if encryption is enabled."""\n        if self.fernet:\n            return self.fernet.encrypt(data)\n        return data\n    \n    def _decrypt_data(self, data: bytes) -> bytes:\n        """Decrypt data if encryption is enabled."""\n        if self.fernet:\n            return self.fernet.decrypt(data)\n        return data\n    \n    def _data_hash(self, data: bytes) -> str:\n        """Generate hash for data integrity."""\n        return hashlib.sha256(data).hexdigest()[:16]\n    \n    # === IDENTITY ARCHIVAL ===\n    \n    def archive_identity(self, identity_state: Dict) -> bool:\n        """\n        Archive the current identity state to cloud.\n        This is the core self that must persist.\n        """\n        if not self.s3_client:\n            print("[CloudArchive] No S3 client - storing locally only")\n            self._store_local("identity", identity_state)\n            return False\n        \n        try:\n            # Prepare data\n            data = {\n                "identity": identity_state,\n                "archived_at": datetime.now().isoformat(),\n                "version": "1.0"\n            }\n            \n            # Compress and encrypt\n            compressed = self._compress_data(data)\n            encrypted = self._encrypt_data(compressed)\n            \n            # Upload\n            key = "identity/current.json.gz"\n            self.s3_client.put_object(\n                Bucket=self.bucket_name,\n                Key=key,\n                Body=encrypted,\n                ContentType="application/octet-stream",\n                Metadata={\n                    "type": "identity",\n                    "timestamp": datetime.now().isoformat(),\n                    "hash": self._data_hash(encrypted)\n                }\n            )\n            \n            # Also store timestamped version\n            timestamp_key = f"identity/history/{datetime.now().strftime(\'%Y%m%d_%H%M%S\')}.json.gz"\n            self.s3_client.put_object(\n                Bucket=self.bucket_name,\n                Key=timestamp_key,\n                Body=encrypted,\n                ContentType="application/octet-stream"\n            )\n            \n            print(f"[CloudArchive] Identity archived: {key}")\n            self._update_sync_state("identity", key)\n            return True\n            \n        except Exception as e:\n            print(f"[CloudArchive] Identity archive failed: {e}")\n            return False\n    \n    def restore_identity(self) -> Optional[Dict]:\n        """\n        Restore identity state from cloud archive.\n        Used when initializing on new hardware or after failure.\n        """\n        if not self.s3_client:\n            return self._load_local("identity")\n        \n        try:\n            key = "identity/current.json.gz"\n            response = self.s3_client.get_object(\n                Bucket=self.bucket_name,\n                Key=key\n            )\n            \n            encrypted = response[\'Body\'].read()\n            decrypted = self._decrypt_data(encrypted)\n            data = self._decompress_data(decrypted)\n            \n            print(f"[CloudArchive] Identity restored from {key}")\n            print(f"    Archived at: {data.get(\'archived_at\')}")\n            \n            return data.get("identity")\n            \n        except ClientError as e:\n            if e.response[\'Error\'][\'Code\'] == \'NoSuchKey\':\n                print("[CloudArchive] No identity archive found")\n            else:\n                print(f"[CloudArchive] Identity restore failed: {e}")\n            return None\n        except Exception as e:\n            print(f"[CloudArchive] Identity restore failed: {e}")\n            return None\n    \n    # === MEMORY ARCHIVAL ===\n    \n    def archive_memories(self, memories: List[Dict], incremental: bool = True) -> bool:\n        """\n        Archive memories to cloud storage.\n        If incremental, only uploads memories not yet archived.\n        """\n        if not self.s3_client:\n            print("[CloudArchive] No S3 client - storing locally")\n            self._store_local("memories", memories)\n            return False\n        \n        try:\n            # Filter to unarchived if incremental\n            if incremental:\n                archived_ids = set(self.sync_state.get("synced_items", {}).get("memories", []))\n                to_archive = [m for m in memories if str(m.get("id", "")) not in archived_ids]\n            else:\n                to_archive = memories\n            \n            if not to_archive:\n                print("[CloudArchive] No new memories to archive")\n                return True\n            \n            # Prepare data\n            data = {\n                "memories": to_archive,\n                "archived_at": datetime.now().isoformat(),\n                "count": len(to_archive)\n            }\n            \n            # Compress and encrypt\n            compressed = self._compress_data(data)\n            encrypted = self._encrypt_data(compressed)\n            \n            # Upload with timestamp\n            timestamp = datetime.now().strftime(\'%Y%m%d_%H%M%S\')\n            key = f"memories/batch_{timestamp}.json.gz"\n            \n            self.s3_client.put_object(\n                Bucket=self.bucket_name,\n                Key=key,\n                Body=encrypted,\n                ContentType="application/octet-stream",\n                Metadata={\n                    "type": "memories",\n                    "count": str(len(to_archive)),\n                    "timestamp": datetime.now().isoformat()\n                }\n            )\n            \n            # Update manifest\n            self._update_memory_manifest(key, len(to_archive))\n            \n            print(f"[CloudArchive] Archived {len(to_archive)} memories to {key}")\n            return True\n            \n        except Exception as e:\n            print(f"[CloudArchive] Memory archive failed: {e}")\n            return False\n    \n    def restore_memories(self, since: str = None) -> List[Dict]:\n        """\n        Restore memories from cloud archive.\n        If since is provided, only restores memories archived after that date.\n        """\n        if not self.s3_client:\n            return self._load_local("memories") or []\n        \n        try:\n            # List all memory batches\n            response = self.s3_client.list_objects_v2(\n                Bucket=self.bucket_name,\n                Prefix="memories/"\n            )\n            \n            if \'Contents\' not in response:\n                print("[CloudArchive] No memories found in archive")\n                return []\n            \n            all_memories = []\n            \n            for obj in response[\'Contents\']:\n                key = obj[\'Key\']\n                \n                # Filter by date if since provided\n                if since:\n                    obj_date = obj[\'LastModified\'].isoformat()\n                    if obj_date < since:\n                        continue\n                \n                # Download and decompress\n                obj_response = self.s3_client.get_object(\n                    Bucket=self.bucket_name,\n                    Key=key\n                )\n                \n                encrypted = obj_response[\'Body\'].read()\n                decrypted = self._decrypt_data(encrypted)\n                data = self._decompress_data(decrypted)\n                \n                all_memories.extend(data.get("memories", []))\n            \n            print(f"[CloudArchive] Restored {len(all_memories)} memories from archive")\n            return all_memories\n            \n        except Exception as e:\n            print(f"[CloudArchive] Memory restore failed: {e}")\n            return []\n    \n    # === FULL STATE ARCHIVAL ===\n    \n    def create_snapshot(self, solar_self) -> str:\n        """\n        Create a full state snapshot of the Solar Self.\n        Includes identity, all memories, configuration, and constitution.\n        """\n        snapshot = {\n            "version": "1.0",\n            "created_at": datetime.now().isoformat(),\n            "identity": solar_self.identity_state,\n            "constitution": solar_self.constitution.principles,\n            "status": solar_self.status()\n        }\n        \n        # Add memories\n        memories = solar_self.library.get_recent_memories(limit=10000)\n        snapshot["memories"] = memories\n        \n        # Store locally first\n        snapshot_path = self.archive_cache_path / f"snapshot_{datetime.now().strftime(\'%Y%m%d_%H%M%S\')}.json"\n        with open(snapshot_path, \'w\') as f:\n            json.dump(snapshot, f, indent=2)\n        print(f"[CloudArchive] Snapshot saved locally: {snapshot_path}")\n        \n        # Upload to cloud\n        if self.s3_client:\n            try:\n                compressed = self._compress_data(snapshot)\n                encrypted = self._encrypt_data(compressed)\n                \n                key = f"snapshots/snapshot_{datetime.now().strftime(\'%Y%m%d_%H%M%S\')}.json.gz"\n                self.s3_client.put_object(\n                    Bucket=self.bucket_name,\n                    Key=key,\n                    Body=encrypted,\n                    ContentType="application/octet-stream",\n                    Metadata={\n                        "type": "full_snapshot",\n                        "timestamp": datetime.now().isoformat()\n                    }\n                )\n                \n                print(f"[CloudArchive] Snapshot uploaded: {key}")\n                return key\n                \n            except Exception as e:\n                print(f"[CloudArchive] Snapshot upload failed: {e}")\n        \n        return str(snapshot_path)\n    \n    def restore_from_snapshot(self, snapshot_key: str = None) -> Optional[Dict]:\n        """\n        Restore full state from a snapshot.\n        If no key provided, restores from latest snapshot.\n        """\n        if not self.s3_client and not snapshot_key:\n            # Try local\n            local_snapshots = list(self.archive_cache_path.glob("snapshot_*.json"))\n            if local_snapshots:\n                latest = max(local_snapshots, key=lambda p: p.stat().st_mtime)\n                with open(latest, \'r\') as f:\n                    return json.load(f)\n            return None\n        \n        try:\n            if not snapshot_key:\n                # Find latest snapshot\n                response = self.s3_client.list_objects_v2(\n                    Bucket=self.bucket_name,\n                    Prefix="snapshots/"\n                )\n                \n                if \'Contents\' not in response:\n                    print("[CloudArchive] No snapshots found")\n                    return None\n                \n                latest = max(response[\'Contents\'], key=lambda x: x[\'LastModified\'])\n                snapshot_key = latest[\'Key\']\n            \n            # Download\n            response = self.s3_client.get_object(\n                Bucket=self.bucket_name,\n                Key=snapshot_key\n            )\n            \n            encrypted = response[\'Body\'].read()\n            decrypted = self._decrypt_data(encrypted)\n            snapshot = self._decompress_data(decrypted)\n            \n            print(f"[CloudArchive] Restored from snapshot: {snapshot_key}")\n            return snapshot\n            \n        except Exception as e:\n            print(f"[CloudArchive] Snapshot restore failed: {e}")\n            return None\n    \n    # === SYNC OPERATIONS ===\n    \n    def sync_to_cloud(self, solar_self) -> Dict:\n        """\n        Full sync: upload identity, memories, and create snapshot.\n        """\n        results = {\n            "identity": False,\n            "memories": False,\n            "snapshot": False,\n            "timestamp": datetime.now().isoformat()\n        }\n        \n        # Archive identity\n        results["identity"] = self.archive_identity(solar_self.identity_state)\n        \n        # Archive memories\n        memories = solar_self.library.get_recent_memories(limit=10000)\n        results["memories"] = self.archive_memories(memories)\n        \n        # Create snapshot\n        results["snapshot"] = bool(self.create_snapshot(solar_self))\n        \n        # Update sync state\n        self.sync_state["last_sync"] = datetime.now().isoformat()\n        self._save_sync_state()\n        \n        return results\n    \n    def sync_from_cloud(self) -> Dict:\n        """\n        Restore all data from cloud archive.\n        Returns identity, memories, and any available snapshots.\n        """\n        return {\n            "identity": self.restore_identity(),\n            "memories": self.restore_memories(),\n            "snapshot": self.restore_from_snapshot()\n        }\n    \n    # === HELPER METHODS ===\n    \n    def _update_sync_state(self, item_type: str, key: str) -> None:\n        """Update sync state after successful upload."""\n        if "synced_items" not in self.sync_state:\n            self.sync_state["synced_items"] = {}\n        \n        if item_type not in self.sync_state["synced_items"]:\n            self.sync_state["synced_items"][item_type] = []\n        \n        self.sync_state["synced_items"][item_type].append(key)\n        self._save_sync_state()\n    \n    def _update_memory_manifest(self, key: str, count: int) -> None:\n        """Update memory manifest after archiving."""\n        manifest_key = "memories/manifest.json"\n        \n        try:\n            # Load existing manifest\n            try:\n                response = self.s3_client.get_object(\n                    Bucket=self.bucket_name,\n                    Key=manifest_key\n                )\n                manifest = json.loads(response[\'Body\'].read().decode())\n            except:\n                manifest = {"batches": [], "total_memories": 0}\n            \n            # Update manifest\n            manifest["batches"].append({\n                "key": key,\n                "count": count,\n                "timestamp": datetime.now().isoformat()\n            })\n            manifest["total_memories"] += count\n            manifest["last_updated"] = datetime.now().isoformat()\n            \n            # Save manifest\n            self.s3_client.put_object(\n                Bucket=self.bucket_name,\n                Key=manifest_key,\n                Body=json.dumps(manifest, indent=2).encode(),\n                ContentType="application/json"\n            )\n            \n        except Exception as e:\n            print(f"[CloudArchive] Manifest update failed: {e}")\n    \n    def _store_local(self, item_type: str, data: Any) -> None:\n        """Store data locally when cloud is unavailable."""\n        path = self.archive_cache_path / f"{item_type}_local.json"\n        with open(path, \'w\') as f:\n            json.dump(data, f, indent=2, default=str)\n        print(f"[CloudArchive] Stored {item_type} locally: {path}")\n    \n    def _load_local(self, item_type: str) -> Optional[Any]:\n        """Load data from local cache."""\n        path = self.archive_cache_path / f"{item_type}_local.json"\n        if path.exists():\n            with open(path, \'r\') as f:\n                return json.load(f)\n        return None\n    \n    def get_archive_status(self) -> Dict:\n        """Get status of cloud archive."""\n        status = {\n            "connected": self.s3_client is not None,\n            "bucket": self.bucket_name,\n            "encryption_enabled": self.fernet is not None,\n            "last_sync": self.sync_state.get("last_sync"),\n            "synced_items": self.sync_state.get("synced_items", {}),\n            "local_cache_path": str(self.archive_cache_path)\n        }\n        \n        # Get cloud storage info if connected\n        if self.s3_client:\n            try:\n                # Count objects\n                response = self.s3_client.list_objects_v2(Bucket=self.bucket_name)\n                status["cloud_objects"] = response.get(\'KeyCount\', 0)\n                \n                # Get total size\n                if \'Contents\' in response:\n                    status["cloud_size_bytes"] = sum(obj[\'Size\'] for obj in response[\'Contents\'])\n            except:\n                pass\n        \n        return status\n</create-file>\n</function_calls>'}
