{'role': 'assistant', 'content': 'Now create a setup guide for cloud storage.\n\n<function_calls>\n<create-file file_path="braided_mind/tools/CLOUD_SETUP.md">\n# Cloud Archive Setup Guide\n\nThe Braided Mind can sync its identity and memories to cloud storage for long-term persistence. This enables:\n\n- **Disaster recovery** - Restore your AI if hardware fails\n- **Cross-device sync** - Access the same identity from multiple machines\n- **Long-term archival** - Memories persist indefinitely\n\n## Free Tier Options\n\n### Option 1: Cloudflare R2 (Recommended)\n- **Free**: 10GB storage, no egress fees\n- **Cost**: $0 beyond free tier\n- **Sign up**: https://dash.cloudflare.com/sign-up/r2\n\n### Option 2: Backblaze B2\n- **Free**: 10GB storage\n- **Egress**: First 1GB/day free\n- **Sign up**: https://www.backblaze.com/b2/sign-up.html\n\n### Option 3: AWS S3\n- **Free**: 5GB for 12 months (AWS Free Tier)\n- **Note**: Egress fees apply\n- **Sign up**: https://aws.amazon.com/free\n\n## Setup Instructions (Cloudflare R2)\n\n### Step 1: Create R2 Bucket\n\n1. Go to https://dash.cloudflare.com\n2. Navigate to R2 Object Storage\n3. Click "Create bucket"\n4. Name it something like `braided-mind-archive`\n5. Choose a location close to you\n\n### Step 2: Create API Token\n\n1. In R2, go to "Manage R2 API Tokens"\n2. Click "Create API token"\n3. Settings:\n   - **Name**: `braided-mind-token`\n   - **Permissions**: Object Read & Write\n   - **TTL**: Leave blank (no expiration)\n4. Click "Create API Token"\n5. **Copy these values** (shown only once!):\n   - Access Key ID\n   - Secret Access Key\n   - Endpoint URL (looks like: `https://<account-id>.r2.cloudflarestorage.com`)\n\n### Step 3: Configure Environment\n\nCreate or edit `.env` file in your braided_mind directory:\n\n```env\n# Hugging Face Token\nHUGGING_FACE_HUB_TOKEN=your_hf_token_here\n\n# Cloud Archive Configuration\nARCHIVE_BUCKET=braided-mind-archive\nARCHIVE_ENDPOINT=https://<account-id>.r2.cloudflarestorage.com\nARCHIVE_ACCESS_KEY=your_access_key_id\nARCHIVE_SECRET_KEY=your_secret_access_key\nARCHIVE_REGION=auto\n\n# Optional: Encryption key (generate your own)\n# Run: python -c "from cryptography.fernet import Fernet; print(Fernet.generate_key().decode())"\nARCHIVE_ENCRYPTION_KEY=your_generated_encryption_key\n```\n\n### Step 4: Test Connection\n\n```bash\npython main.py\n# At the prompt:\nstatus\n# Check that cloud archive shows "connected: True"\n```\n\n## Setup Instructions (Backblaze B2)\n\n### Step 1: Create Bucket\n\n1. Go to https://www.backblaze.com/b2/buckets.html\n2. Click "Create a Bucket"\n3. Name: `braided-mind-archive`\n4. Keep defaults, create\n\n### Step 2: Create Application Key\n\n1. Go to App Keys under Account\n2. Click "Add a New Application Key"\n3. Name: `braided-mind-key`\n4. Allow access to specific bucket: `braided-mind-archive`\n5. Access: Read and Write\n6. Create and copy:\n   - keyID (Access Key)\n   - applicationKey (Secret Key)\n\n### Step 3: Configure\n\n```env\nARCHIVE_BUCKET=braided-mind-archive\nARCHIVE_ENDPOINT=https://s3.us-west-004.backblazeb2.com  # Use your bucket\'s endpoint\nARCHIVE_ACCESS_KEY=your_key_id\nARCHIVE_SECRET_KEY=your_application_key\n```\n\n## Usage\n\nOnce configured, use these commands:\n\n```\n# Sync identity and memories to cloud\nsync\n\n# Create full backup snapshot\nbackup\n\n# Restore from cloud archive\nrestore\n```\n\n## What Gets Archived\n\n### Always Synced\n- **Identity State** - Your core self, goals, focus, thought count\n- **Recent Memories** - Significant learnings and experiences\n\n### On Backup\n- **Full Snapshot** - Complete state including constitution\n- **All Memories** - Everything stored in the library\n\n## Storage Estimates\n\n| Content | Size Estimate |\n|---------|---------------|\n| Identity state | ~10 KB |\n| 100 memories | ~50 KB |\n| 1000 memories | ~500 KB |\n| Full snapshot | ~1-5 MB |\n\nWith 10GB free storage, you can store:\n- ~200,000 memories\n- ~2,000 full snapshots\n\n## Security Notes\n\n1. **Encryption**: If you set `ARCHIVE_ENCRYPTION_KEY`, all data is encrypted before upload\n2. **Access Keys**: Never commit `.env` to git or share publicly\n3. **Bucket Privacy**: Keep buckets private (default setting)\n\n## Troubleshooting\n\n### "Cloud archive not configured"\n- Check that all `ARCHIVE_*` environment variables are set\n- Restart the system after updating `.env`\n\n### "Connection refused" / "Access Denied"\n- Verify Access Key and Secret Key are correct\n- Check bucket name matches exactly\n- Verify endpoint URL is correct for your provider\n\n### "Sync failed"\n- Check internet connection\n- Verify bucket permissions (Read/Write)\n- Check Cloudflare/Backblaze status pages\n\n## Cross-Device Setup\n\nTo use the same identity on multiple machines:\n\n1. Set up Braided Mind on both machines\n2. Configure the same cloud archive on both\n3. On the first machine: run `sync`\n4. On the second machine: run `restore`\n5. Both now share the same identity and memories\n\nNote: Sync is not automatic. Remember to `sync` before switching machines.\n</create-file>\n</function_calls>'}
